# dsh-guard is plain text and JavaScript; it holds no line-ending-sensitive
# vendored bytes the way dsh-subagent-permissions does, but `* -text` keeps
# checkouts byte-identical across platforms, which is what the `.ps1` scripts and
# the Chinese READMEs need (a CRLF rewrite would also invalidate the UTF-8 BOM
# handling those scripts depend on).
* -text

# Windows PowerShell 5.1 cannot parse a UTF-8 script without a BOM, and these
# four scripts carry Chinese text. Keep them out of any auto-detection or
# normalization that might strip the BOM or rewrite the encoding.
*.ps1 -text working-tree-encoding=UTF-8

# Binary artefacts never belong in a text diff.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
